From 4cb0b5a7262f1a679a50b2faec67d131df2a0a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] kd: Draw the console on a linear framebuffer when there
 is no text mode

Firmware such as coreboot with a framebuffer, or UEFI, leaves the display
in a graphics mode with nothing behind the EGA text buffer at 0xb8000, so
the kernel console writes are silently lost and the screen keeps showing
whatever the boot loader drew last.

When the multiboot information describes an RGB framebuffer, map it and
point the kd display layer at an in-memory EGA-style text page instead.
Every change to that page is painted onto the framebuffer with an 8x16
code page 437 font rendered from GNU Unifont, keeping the 80x25 cell
model the rest of kd.c relies on.  Only cells whose contents changed are
repainted.  The EGA path is unchanged when the boot loader reports text
mode or no video information at all.
---
